The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**`. That path
does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group — placing files there would not
compile. The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/`,
where the landed sibling P7 battery pages ship (BatteryCellsPage, BatteryDegradationPage,
SleepEfficiencyPage — ledger status=done), and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml
source path (createIntermediateGroups: true). Page hosting uses the proven `*RouteRegistration`
pattern chained in `Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift`. Tests live in `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Battery/`.
The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Battery/**` — the faithful equivalent of
the prompt's `Features/Battery`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only
deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9. It is identical to the
reconciliation used by every landed p4-apple P7 page.

The `.energy` AppRoute case already existed (AppRoute.swift) with `/energy` + `/battery` +
`/battery/health` deep-link aliases (AppRouteParser) but had NO registered host; this prompt wires it.

