================================================================================
SUMMARY
================================================================================
A SwiftUI + Apple-HIG parity of the web EnergyPage (route /energy), adaptive across macOS + iOS
(ADR-002/006). The page binds an injectable EnergyDataSource seam (loadVehicles/loadStats/loadSessions/
loadTelemetry — the web useSelectedVehicle + useEnergyStats + useChargingSessionsPaginated +
useChargingTelemetryLatest queries) through the @Observable EnergyPageModel; the view holds no
networking (ADR-004) and every visible quantity is SI on disk, converted only at the render boundary
via the shared Units facade (ADR-005). It reproduces the web chrome (Energy-Intelligence title +
subtitle + header VehicleSelect), the four hero gauges (or the honest empty hero when the vehicle has
no energy data — web hasNoEnergyData, never four misleading zeros), the six quick-metric chips, the
lifetime panel (live lifetime-kWh + selected-window energy), the two cost-vs-gas comparison cards, the
four P3 charts (TSComposedChart energy+efficiency, TSAreaChart efficiency+distance, TSBarChart
time-of-day energy+count with off-peak/solar tips, TSPieChart charger-type donut + per-category list),
and the seven-column recent-sessions TSDataTable — all from the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no
hand-rolled glass, no direct Charts/recharts, no WKWebView). Every data source implements
loading/empty/error/success and every section its own empty state; all 56 visible strings resolve from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (55 added; common.noData already present). The web RadialGauge
is reproduced natively as EnergyGauge (value+unit centre) since the shared TSRadialGauge renders a
percentage; the web dual-axis charts become single-axis with both series converted to display units so
both stay visible. Verified GREEN: swiftlint --strict (0), placeholder gate (0), the full macOS app
xcodebuild (** BUILD SUCCEEDED **, Swift 6 strict-concurrency complete, 0 diagnostics in any file), the
iOS app-target compile of every Energy file (0 errors), and an executed pure-logic harness (35/35). The
shared XCTest bundle is pre-existing RED ONLY due to two unrelated, out-of-scope test files (covenant #7);
ZERO diagnostics in any Energy file.

